{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Rooted deep in the soil of Judah
The branch of Jerahmeel [Bb]grew
[Dm]Hezron's firstborn led the way
Ram [C]and Bunah in their [Dm]day
Oren and O[C]zem stood [Dm]beside
Ahi[C]jah walk[Bb]ing with [Dm]pride
Another [C]wife [F]named A[Bbmaj7]tarah
[Dm]Mother [C]of Onam in the [Dm]earth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Shammai and [C]Jada were [Dm]born
From Onam's [C]line in the [Bb]dawn
Sham[Dm]mai's sons [C]were Nadab [F]and A[Bbmaj7]bishur
[Dm]Abis[C]hur's wife bore the [Dm]fruit
Abihail [C]gave birth to Ah[Dm]ban
Molid [C]joined in the [Bb]clan
Nad[Dm]ab's [C]sons were Se[F]led and [Bbmaj7]Appaim
[Dm]Seled [C]died without chil[Dm]dren's claim
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But [Bb]Appaim carried [F]the name
[Bb]Sole heir in the house of [F]fame
The [Bb]son of [C]Appaim was [Dm]Ishi
Who [Bb]walked in [C]the faithful [Dm]day
[Bb]Sheshan [C]came after Is[Dm]hi
And [Bb]Ahlai [C]closed the [Dm]way
The [Bb]ge[C]nealogy [Fmaj7/A]stands [Bbmaj7]and tells
Of the tribe [C]that never [Dm]falls
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The sons of [C]Sheshan followed [Dm]on
Ahlai [C]kept the tra[Bb]dition
Re[Dm]cor[C]ding names for in[F]heri[Bbmaj7]tance
[Dm]Tribal [C]rights in the [Dm]land
From Judah down [C]through Jerah[Dm]meel
The lines were [C]kept whole and [Bb]real
No [Dm]broth[C]er's line was [F]lost in [Bbmaj7]the dark [Dm]
[C]For Appaim left his [Dm]mark
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But Ap[Bb]paim carried the [F]name
[Bb]Sole heir in the house of [F]fame
The [Bb]son of [C]Appaim was [Dm]Ishi
Who [Bb]walked in [C]the faithful [Dm]day
[Bb]Sheshan [C]came after Is[Dm]hi
And [Bb]Ahlai [C]closed the [Dm]way
The [Bb]geneal[C]ogy [Fmaj7/A]stands [Bbmaj7]and tells
Of the tribe [C]that never [Dm]falls
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Son of [C]Appaim, Is[Dm]hi
The [Bb]line [C]continues [Dm]on
[Bb]Sheshan, [C]Ahlai, the [Dm]end
[Bb]Of [C]the chronicle's [Dm]song
{end_of_verse}
